STEP 3 - THE DECOMPOSITION THE CLAIM DOES NOT DO: ROYALTY vs LICENSE  [source A, Note 4]
============================================================================================
                                        FY26      FY25     delta     %chg
External ROYALTY                       2,123     1,763      +360   +20.4%
External LICENSE & other               1,298     1,421      -123    -8.7%
Related-party ROYALTY (Arm China)        490       405       +85   +21.0%
Related-party LICENSE & other          1,009       418      +591  +141.4%
TOTAL ROYALTY                          2,613     2,168      +445   +20.5%   <-- 0% SoftBank consulting in this line
TOTAL LICENSE & OTHER                  2,307     1,839      +468   +25.4%

Royalty share of total revenue: FY26 53.1%, FY25 54.1%
SoftBank consulting delta (+$558.9m) vs TOTAL license&other delta (+$468m): the consulting fee is 119% of the license line's growth.
=> License & other EX-SoftBank-consulting: $1,602.6m vs $1,693.5m = -5.4%  (i.e. it SHRANK)

So the damage is confined to the LICENSE line. Royalty revenue -- the line that actually
measures Arm-based chips SHIPPING in end products -- grew +20.5% with zero SoftBank content.
Note 4 fn(1): point-in-time license revenue $1,372m -> $1,227m (-10.6%); over-time $467m -> $1,080m (+131%).

