STEP 7 - FORWARD TEST: DOES THE 'CONTAMINATION' REVERSE?  [source E, 6-K FY27 Q1]
============================================================================================
FY27 Q1 total revenue      $1,289m vs $1,053m = +22.4%
FY27 Q1 related-party      $388m vs $328m = +18.3%  (filing text: 'increased $60 million, or 18%')
FY27 Q1 EXTERNAL revenue   $901m vs $725m = +24.3%
FY27 Q1 SoftBank consulting $192.9m vs $126.1m = +53.0%  -> annualising ~$772m

=> In the MOST RECENT reported quarter the sign FLIPS: external revenue grows FASTER than
   related-party revenue. The FY26 'external only +7%' is a fiscal-year artifact of the
   lumpy license line, not a persistent condition. And the SoftBank fee is RECURRING and
   GROWING, not a one-off that mechanically reverses out of the growth rate.

============================================================================================
STEP 8 - CASH QUALITY OF THE SOFTBANK REVENUE  [sources A, B]
============================================================================================
Current contract assets from the SoftBank affiliate: $145.5m @2025-03-31 -> $645.8m @2026-03-31
Claim's framing: $645.8m / FY26 revenue $704.4m = 91.7% 'unbilled'  -> arithmetic CORRECT
But the balance is CUMULATIVE, not FY26-specific: cumulative revenue recognised $849.9m, contract asset $645.8m => $204.1m (24%) has converted out of contract assets.
[B] FY25 20-F: 'As of March 31, 2025, the Company had contract assets of $145.5 million and
    did not have any accounts receivable' -> 100% of the FY25 fee was ALSO unbilled, yet [A]
    reports no impairment of it. No expected-credit-loss allowance against the SoftBank
    affiliate is disclosed in [A] (contrast: Arm China ECL $12.3m FY26 / $16.0m FY25).
[A] Item 7B: a statement of work was restructured into 'a fixed payment amount of $300
    million, which will be paid during the fiscal year ending March 31, 2027.'
